        ('A chemical bond formed by the complete transfer of electrons from one atom to another is called a(n)', ['covalent bond', 'ionic bond', 'metallic bond', 'van der Waals bond'], 1, 'Ionic bonds form through electron transfer, creating oppositely charged ions that attract each other.'),
        ('The bonds between hydrogen and oxygen in a water molecule are', ['ionic', 'covalent', 'metallic', 'purely van der Waals'], 1, 'Water molecules are held together internally by polar covalent O-H bonds.'),
