        ('A segment of DNA that codes for a particular protein or trait is called a', ['chromosome', 'gene', 'nucleus', 'enzyme'], 1, 'A gene is a specific DNA sequence that codes for a protein or functional product.'),
        ('DNA is organized into structures called', ['ribosomes', 'chromosomes', 'vacuoles', 'chloroplasts'], 1, 'DNA is packaged together with proteins into chromosomes within the nucleus.'),
        ('In genetics, an allele that is expressed even when only one copy is present is called', ['recessive', 'dominant', 'mutant', 'homozygous'], 1, 'A dominant allele shows its effect even in a single (heterozygous) copy.'),
        ('Gregor Mendel is best known for his foundational work in', ['cell theory', 'genetics and heredity', 'evolution by natural selection', 'the germ theory of disease'], 1, "Mendel's pea plant experiments established the basic laws of inheritance."),
        ('The observable physical traits of an organism are referred to as its', ['genotype', 'phenotype', 'karyotype', 'genome'], 1, 'Phenotype refers to the visible/measurable characteristics resulting from genotype and environment.'),
