        ('Photosynthesis converts carbon dioxide and water, using light energy, into glucose and', ['nitrogen', 'oxygen', 'methane', 'ozone'], 1, 'Photosynthesis releases oxygen as a byproduct while producing glucose.'),
        ('The tissue responsible for transporting water and minerals upward in a plant is the', ['phloem', 'xylem', 'epidermis', 'cortex'], 1, 'Xylem tissue conducts water and dissolved minerals from roots to the rest of the plant.'),
        ('The tissue responsible for transporting food (sugars) throughout a plant is the', ['xylem', 'phloem', 'cambium', 'cuticle'], 1, 'Phloem transports the products of photosynthesis, mainly sugars, around the plant.'),
